{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py`. It only did `value // width`, so a value exactly on the upper range (e.g. `30` with width `10` and 3 buckets) produced index `3` instead of the last valid bucket `2`. `histogram_summary` then indexed `counts[3]` and raised an `IndexError`, and those top-edge values never landed in the last bar.\n\nThe fix clamps any index `>= n_buckets` to `n_buckets - 1`, matching the function’s docstring:\n\n```10:14:repo/histogram.py\n    idx = value // width\n    if idx >= n_buckets:\n        return n_buckets - 1\n    return idx\n```\n\nAll tests pass, and a quick check with `[10, 20, 30]` now returns `{'n': 3, 'counts': [0, 1, 2]}` without error (20 and 30 both count in the last bucket)."}]},"session_id":"a3542725-8045-4d2c-8833-3ec85a5c6dad"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":41412,"duration_api_ms":41412,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for histogram chart implementation and last-bucket handling.\n\n\nIdentifying the issue: `bucket_of` uses integer division without clamping, so values on the top edge (e.g. 30 with width 10 and 3 buckets) return index 3 and cause an IndexError in `histogram_summary`.\n\n\nThe problem was in `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py`. It only did `value // width`, so a value exactly on the upper range (e.g. `30` with width `10` and 3 buckets) produced index `3` instead of the last valid bucket `2`. `histogram_summary` then indexed `counts[3]` and raised an `IndexError`, and those top-edge values never landed in the last bar.\n\nThe fix clamps any index `>= n_buckets` to `n_buckets - 1`, matching the function’s docstring:\n\n```10:14:repo/histogram.py\n    idx = value // width\n    if idx >= n_buckets:\n        return n_buckets - 1\n    return idx\n```\n\nAll tests pass, and a quick check with `[10, 20, 30]` now returns `{'n': 3, 'counts': [0, 1, 2]}` without error (20 and 30 both count in the last bucket).","session_id":"a3542725-8045-4d2c-8833-3ec85a5c6dad","request_id":"feb92da0-0346-4d53-9142-ad633f429cb7","usage":{"inputTokens":11801,"outputTokens":1672,"cacheReadTokens":89390,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
